WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.990
Truecell turns difficult PDFs and scans into reviewable spreadsheet data with source evidence.

2
00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:11.780
A plausible misplaced number can corrupt decisions, so extraction alone is not enough.

3
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:17.571
Everything runs locally on CPU, without an API key or cloud AI upload.

4
00:00:17.571 --> 00:00:22.916
Open PDFs or supported images, with PDF intake up to 200 pages.

5
00:00:22.916 --> 00:00:29.151
Before extraction, Truecell profiles scripts, text health, blur, skew, rotation, perspective, and table likelihood.

6
00:00:29.151 --> 00:00:34.051
Native PDF strategies, bundled RapidOCR, and installed Tesseract produce independent candidates.

7
00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:38.950
Every candidate, rank, reason, and missing capability appears in Page Audit.

8
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:44.740
This dummy bank statement extracts successfully, but its quality status is Needs review.

9
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.640
The priority queue combines validation failures, uncertain readings, and unlocated evidence.

10
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:54.984
Selecting a finding jumps to its table cell and exact source location.

11
00:00:54.984 --> 00:01:00.329
Evidence retains page, bounding box, original reading, engine, alternatives, and confidence meaning.

12
00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:04.783
Repeated values reveal a running-balance relationship without fixed financial headings.

13
00:01:04.783 --> 00:01:09.683
Fifteen of seventeen rows agree; printed 1081 breaks two adjacent equations.

14
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:14.582
Truecell proposes 1064 and shows both equation instances supporting the suggestion.

15
00:01:14.582 --> 00:01:20.372
Preview evaluates the proposal on a disposable copy while saved data remains unchanged.

16
00:01:20.372 --> 00:01:25.717
The failures would clear, but agreement is evidence, never permission to overwrite.

17
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:31.507
After source inspection, the reviewer enters a reason and explicitly applies the correction.

18
00:01:31.507 --> 00:01:35.516
History preserves the original value, replacement, timestamp, and explanation.

19
00:01:35.516 --> 00:01:40.861
Reviewed export remains locked until every priority item is resolved and attested.

20
00:01:40.861 --> 00:01:46.206
A five-page raster-only case tests repeated headers and rows split across pages.

21
00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:51.996
Truecell reconstructs twelve columns, removes four repeated headers, and recovers both split rows.

22
00:01:51.996 --> 00:01:57.786
The join receipt exposes every contributing page, join, removed header, and recovered fragment.

23
00:01:57.786 --> 00:02:04.022
It also handles borderless tables, merged headers, wrapped values, empty columns, and multiple tables.

24
00:02:04.022 --> 00:02:09.812
Source-backed vertical groups and nested items are preserved; ambiguity is routed to review.

25
00:02:09.812 --> 00:02:14.711
Search spans every column while retaining each result's original row identity.

26
00:02:14.711 --> 00:02:20.056
Selecting invoice 800 goes to page 50 and highlights its source value.

27
00:02:20.056 --> 00:02:25.401
Filtering never breaks the evidence link between displayed cells and original pages.

28
00:02:25.401 --> 00:02:30.746
Honest states distinguish complete, partial, failed, needs rescan, needs review, and reviewed.

29
00:02:30.746 --> 00:02:37.872
If a page fails, later pages continue; checkpoints resume only when source and runtime still match.

30
00:02:37.872 --> 00:02:42.772
Saved local workspaces preserve extraction, corrections, and review history across restarts.

31
00:02:42.772 --> 00:02:47.671
Export working data through Excel, CSV, JSON, or the local API.

32
00:02:47.671 --> 00:02:53.907
The workbook includes data, evidence, validation, joins, page audit, constraints, provenance, corrections, and verification.

33
00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:58.806
Linked spreadsheet cells open their evidence row beside the processing trail.

34
00:02:58.806 --> 00:03:04.151
Across disclosed development fixtures, all 23 source-bound cases passed their exact checks.

35
00:03:04.151 --> 00:03:11.723
RapidOCR passed five of five scans without Tesseract; the public Unicode audit matched 126 of 126 cells.

36
00:03:11.723 --> 00:03:16.622
The stress fixture recovered 50 pages, 800 rows, and 12 columns.

37
00:03:16.622 --> 00:03:21.076
A 13-page, four-table synthetic case matched 1,092 checked cells exactly.

38
00:03:21.076 --> 00:03:25.976
These are disclosed development results, not universal or unseen-document accuracy claims.

39
00:03:25.976 --> 00:03:31.766
A truth-withheld blind evaluation workflow is ready for independent testing without rerunning extraction.

40
00:03:31.766 --> 00:03:39.338
Truecell ships for Windows, Python, and Docker; the verified build passed 304 Python and 16 frontend tests.

41
00:03:39.338 --> 00:03:45.128
Truecell combines extraction, validation, evidence, human review, and recovery in one local workflow.

42
00:03:45.128 --> 00:03:50.473
Difficult documents become defensible spreadsheets, with uncertainty visible and every decision recorded.

43
00:03:50.473 --> 00:03:52.700
Truecell. Every cell, accounted for.
